          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Insert new Section 11.4 requiring Commerce One to provide up to six months of transition assistance and to return, then delete and certify deletion of, Corio and Customer data on expiry or termination.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We have added a transition-assistance and data-return provision at Section 11.4: on exit, Commerce One provides up to six (6) months of migration assistance at its then-current rates, returns our and our Customers' data within thirty (30) days in a machine-readable format, and then deletes it and certifies deletion. Our playbook requires an orderly exit path for hosted services; we can accept ninety (90) days of assistance as a fallback, and have carved out retention needed for Commerce One's surviving support obligations and applicable law.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0098",
              "numbering": "11.4",
              "text": "11.4 Transition Assistance and Return of Data. Upon expiration or termination of this Agreement for any reason, Commerce One shall, at Corio's request: (a) provide reasonable transition and migration assistance to Corio and its Customers for a period of up to six (6) months at Commerce One's then-current standard rates; (b) within thirty (30) days of Corio's request, return to Corio all data of Corio and its Customers then in Commerce One's possession or control, including data generated through or stored in connection with the MarketSite.net Service, in a commonly used, machine-readable format; and (c) thereafter delete all such data from its systems and certify such deletion to Corio in writing, except to the extent retention is required to perform Commerce One's surviving obligations under this Agreement or by applicable law. This Section 11.4 shall survive the termination or expiration of this Agreement for any reason."
            }
          ]
